{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L4hz36a3MDnWpgSP7zbnz2","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: rel00.0-uc002-format\n     2→title: \"Format output with columns, color, and human-readable sizes\"\n     3→\n     4→summary: |\n     5→  The operator verifies that pkg/format produces correct column layouts, ANSI color\n     6→  sequences, and human-readable size strings. The test exercises each formatting\n     7→  capability in isolation: Columns distributes entries into a grid that fits the terminal\n     8→  width, FileTypeColor returns the correct ANSI escape for each file type, the color\n     9→  override mechanism works for --color=always and --color=never, and HumanSize converts\n    10→  byte counts to human-readable strings matching GNU coreutils behavior.\n    11→\n    12→actor: Human Operator\n    13→\n    14→trigger: |\n    15→  The operator has completed the PRD revision (prd003-format.yaml) and wants to verify\n    16→  that pkg/format satisfies its requirements via unit tests.\n    17→\n    18→flow:\n    19→  - id: F1\n    20→    step: |\n    21→      The operator runs go test ./pkg/format/... which executes the unit tests for\n    22→      pkg/format. Unlike cmd/ packages, pkg/format does not use differential testing\n    23→      because there is no reference binary — it is a library.\n    24→  - id: F2\n    25→    step: |\n    26→      The Columns test creates a list of 20 filenames and calls Columns(entries, 80).\n    27→      The function distributes entries into the maximum number of columns that fit within\n    28→      80 characters, computing column widths from the longest entry in each column.\n    29→  - id: F3\n    30→    step: |\n    31→      The PadRight and PadLeft tests verify that strings are padded to the specified\n    32→      display width using rune count, not byte count.\n    33→  - id: F4\n    34→    step: |\n    35→      The FileTypeColor test calls SetColorEnabled(true), then verifies that each of the\n    36→      eight file types (directory, symlink, executable, block device, character device,\n    37→      socket, pipe, regular) returns the correct ANSI escape sequence per GNU ls defaults.\n    38→  - id: F5\n    39→    step: |\n    40→      The color override test calls SetColorEnabled(false) and verifies that FileTypeColor\n    41→      and Reset return empty strings for all file types. It then calls ResetColorEnabled\n    42→      to restore automatic detection.\n    43→  - id: F6\n    44→    step: |\n    45→      The ColorEnabled test passes an os.Pipe writer and verifies it returns false.\n    46→      It passes a bytes.Buffer and verifies it returns false.\n    47→  - id: F7\n    48→    step: |\n    49→      The HumanSize test verifies binary mode (1024-based): HumanSize(1536, binary)\n    50→      returns \"1.5K\", HumanSize(0, binary) returns \"0\". It verifies SI mode (1000-based):\n    51→      HumanSize(1000000, SI) returns \"1.0MB\".\n    52→\n    53→touchpoints:\n    54→  - T1: \"pkg/format — Columns, PadRight, PadLeft, displayWidth (prd003-format R1)\"\n    55→  - T2: \"pkg/format — FileTypeColor, Reset, ColorEnabled, SetColorEnabled, ResetColorEnabled (prd003-format R2)\"\n    56→  - T3: \"pkg/format — HumanSize (prd003-format R3)\"\n    57→  - T4: \"pkg/sys — IsTerminal, called internally by ColorEnabled\"\n    58→\n    59→success_criteria:\n    60→  - id: S1\n    61→    criterion: Columns(20 filenames, 80) produces a grid where each row fits within 80 characters.\n    62→  - id: S2\n    63→    criterion: PadRight(\"abc\", 10) returns \"abc\" followed by 7 spaces. PadLeft(\"abc\", 10) returns 7 spaces followed by \"abc\".\n    64→  - id: S3\n    65→    criterion: FileTypeColor returns the correct ANSI code for all eight file types when color is enabled.\n    66→  - id: S4\n    67→    criterion: SetColorEnabled(false) suppresses all ANSI output. ResetColorEnabled restores automatic detection.\n    68→  - id: S5\n    69→    criterion: ColorEnabled returns false for pipe and non-*os.File writers.\n    70→  - id: S6\n    71→    criterion: HumanSize(1536, binary) returns \"1.5K\". HumanSize(1000000, SI) returns \"1.0MB\". HumanSize(0, binary) returns \"0\".\n    72→  - id: S7\n    73→    criterion: go test ./pkg/format/... passes with no failures.\n    74→\n    75→out_of_scope:\n    76→  - LS_COLORS environment variable parsing is explicitly excluded from pkg/format.\n    77→  - Terminal hyperlinks are not in scope.\n    78→  - East-asian full-width character width computation is deferred.\n    79→\n    80→test_suite: test-rel00.0\n    81→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"278ea2bf-8175-4107-871d-11b3bb989640","uuid":"f47db51f-80db-4f5e-ba39-2b0e7030734b","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/280/docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc002-format.yaml","content":"id: rel00.0-uc002-format\ntitle: \"Format output with columns, color, and human-readable sizes\"\n\nsummary: |\n  The operator verifies that pkg/format produces correct column layouts, ANSI color\n  sequences, and human-readable size strings. The test exercises each formatting\n  capability in isolation: Columns distributes entries into a grid that fits the terminal\n  width, FileTypeColor returns the correct ANSI escape for each file type, the color\n  override mechanism works for --color=always and --color=never, and HumanSize converts\n  byte counts to human-readable strings matching GNU coreutils behavior.\n\nactor: Human Operator\n\ntrigger: |\n  The operator has completed the PRD revision (prd003-format.yaml) and wants to verify\n  that pkg/format satisfies its requirements via unit tests.\n\nflow:\n  - id: F1\n    step: |\n      The operator runs go test ./pkg/format/... which executes the unit tests for\n      pkg/format. Unlike cmd/ packages, pkg/format does not use differential testing\n      because there is no reference binary — it is a library.\n  - id: F2\n    step: |\n      The Columns test creates a list of 20 filenames and calls Columns(entries, 80).\n      The function distributes entries into the maximum number of columns that fit within\n      80 characters, computing column widths from the longest entry in each column.\n  - id: F3\n    step: |\n      The PadRight and PadLeft tests verify that strings are padded to the specified\n      display width using rune count, not byte count.\n  - id: F4\n    step: |\n      The FileTypeColor test calls SetColorEnabled(true), then verifies that each of the\n      eight file types (directory, symlink, executable, block device, character device,\n      socket, pipe, regular) returns the correct ANSI escape sequence per GNU ls defaults.\n  - id: F5\n    step: |\n      The color override test calls SetColorEnabled(false) and verifies that FileTypeColor\n      and Reset return empty strings for all file types. It then calls ResetColorEnabled\n      to restore automatic detection.\n  - id: F6\n    step: |\n      The ColorEnabled test passes an os.Pipe writer and verifies it returns false.\n      It passes a bytes.Buffer and verifies it returns false.\n  - id: F7\n    step: |\n      The HumanSize test verifies binary mode (1024-based): HumanSize(1536, binary)\n      returns \"1.5K\", HumanSize(0, binary) returns \"0\". It verifies SI mode (1000-based):\n      HumanSize(1000000, SI) returns \"1.0MB\".\n\ntouchpoints:\n  - T1: \"pkg/format — Columns, PadRight, PadLeft, displayWidth (prd003-format R1)\"\n  - T2: \"pkg/format — FileTypeColor, Reset, ColorEnabled, SetColorEnabled, ResetColorEnabled (prd003-format R2)\"\n  - T3: \"pkg/format — HumanSize (prd003-format R3)\"\n  - T4: \"pkg/sys — IsTerminal, called internally by ColorEnabled\"\n\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - id: S1\n    criterion: Columns(20 filenames, 80) produces a grid where each row fits within 80 characters.\n  - id: S2\n    criterion: PadRight(\"abc\", 10) returns \"abc\" followed by 7 spaces. PadLeft(\"abc\", 10) returns 7 spaces followed by \"abc\".\n  - id: S3\n    criterion: FileTypeColor returns the correct ANSI code for all eight file types when color is enabled.\n  - id: S4\n    criterion: SetColorEnabled(false) suppresses all ANSI output. ResetColorEnabled restores automatic detection.\n  - id: S5\n    criterion: ColorEnabled returns false for pipe and non-*os.File writers.\n  - id: S6\n    criterion: HumanSize(1536, binary) returns \"1.5K\". HumanSize(1000000, SI) returns \"1.0MB\". HumanSize(0, binary) returns \"0\".\n  - id: S7\n    criterion: go test ./pkg/format/... passes with no failures.\n\nout_of_scope:\n  - LS_COLORS environment variable parsing is explicitly excluded from pkg/format.\n  - Terminal hyperlinks are not in scope.\n  - East-asian full-width character width computation is deferred.\n\ntest_suite: test-rel00.0\n","numLines":81,"startLine":1,"totalLines":81}}}
